{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":1892526,"ns":0,"title":"Duck test","extract":"The duck test is a frequently cited colloquial example of abductive reasoning. Its usual expression is:\n\nIf it looks like a duck, swims like a duck, and quacks like a duck, then it probably is a duck.","description":"Classification based on observable evidence","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}